    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d314-a2">

                <pb facs="0478" n="382" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg382"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 548.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Lord Salisbury to Mr. White.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-10-05"><hi rendition="#italic">October 5,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge your note
                    of the 28th ultimo, expressing the sympathy of the United States Government at
                    the death of Mr. F. W. Ramsden, late Her Majesty’s consul at Santiago de Cuba,
                    and their appreciation of the services rendered by him in guarding American
                    interests during the recent hostilities with Spain.</p>
                <p>I shall be obliged if you will convey to the United States Secretary of State my
                    thanks for this communication.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Salisbury.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
